format 1

# pklith's own registry: every tracked file type and the hk steps (hk.pkl)
# that check it. `pkli check` judges this repository against it.
#
# The checks are defined locally below until pklith ships a built-in
# catalog. `check` and `fix` are the exact commands of the matching hk.pkl
# steps; `pkli gen` renders them into hk.pklith.pkl.

## checks
id|category|nix|glob|check|fix|env|msg
trailing-whitespace|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util trailing-whitespace --diff {{files}}|hk util trailing-whitespace --fix {{files}}|-|trailing blanks; the pre-commit hook strips them
final-newline|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util end-of-file-fixer --diff {{files}}|hk util end-of-file-fixer --fix {{files}}|-|file must end with a newline
line-endings|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util mixed-line-ending --diff {{files}}|hk util mixed-line-ending --fix {{files}}|-|file mixes CRLF and LF
no-bom|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util check-byte-order-marker {{files}}|-|-|file starts with a byte order marker
no-merge-conflict|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util check-merge-conflict --assume-in-merge {{files}}|-|-|leftover merge conflict markers
no-case-conflict|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util check-case-conflict {{files}}|-|-|two paths differ only by case
no-broken-symlinks|hygiene|-|-|git ls-files -z \| xargs -0 hk util check-symlinks|-|-|a symlink points nowhere
no-large-files|hygiene|-|**/*|scripts/no-large-files.sh {{files}}|-|-|file over its type's size limit
no-private-key|secret|-|**/*|hk util detect-private-key {{files}}|-|-|a private key block is staged
ripsecrets|secret|ripsecrets|**/*|ripsecrets {{files}}|-|-|a token or credential is staged; a false positive goes in .secretsignore
typos|lint|typos|**/*|typos --force-exclude {{files}}|-|-|misspelling; fix it or teach .typos.toml
nixfmt|format|nixfmt|**/*.nix|nixfmt --check {{files}}|nixfmt {{files}}|-|nix file not formatted
taplo|format|taplo|**/*.toml|taplo fmt --check {{files}}|taplo fmt {{files}}|-|TOML not formatted or not parseable
rustfmt|format|rustfmt|**/*.rs|cargo fmt --check|cargo fmt|-|Rust not formatted
clippy|lint|clippy|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, clippy.toml|cargo clippy --all-targets -q -- -D warnings|-|-|clippy finding or a §C code limit exceeded
test|test|cargo-nextest|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock|cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast --status-level fail --final-status-level fail|-|-|a test failed, or the suite is empty
doctest|test|cargo|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml|cargo test --doc -q|-|-|a doc example failed
rustdoc|lint|cargo|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml|cargo doc --no-deps --document-private-items -q|-|RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings|docs do not build cleanly
coverage|coverage|sherd|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, .coverage|sherd coverage --check|-|-|line coverage fell below .coverage
file-ceilings|spec|sherd|**/*.rs|scripts/file-ceilings.sh|-|-|a Rust file is over its token ceiling
shellcheck|lint|shellcheck|.githooks/*, .envrc, **/*.sh|shellcheck --shell=bash {{files}}|-|-|shell script finding
actionlint|lint|actionlint|.github/workflows/*.yml, .github/workflows/*.yaml|actionlint {{files}}|-|-|workflow does not parse or type-check
zizmor|lint|zizmor|.github/workflows/*.yml, .github/workflows/*.yaml|zizmor --offline --no-progress {{files}}|-|-|workflow security finding
links|lint|lychee|**/*.md|git ls-files -z '*.md' \| xargs -0 lychee --offline --no-progress --include-fragments|-|-|a relative link or anchor is broken
mth-fmt|spec|microlith|**/SPEC.md|for f in {{files}}; do mth fmt --check "$f" \|\| exit 1; done|for f in {{files}}; do mth fmt "$f" \|\| exit 1; done|-|SPEC.md is hard-wrapped or over the line cap
mth-check|spec|microlith|**/SPEC.md|for f in {{files}}; do mth check "$f" \|\| exit 1; done|-|-|SPEC.md breaks a structural rule
sherd-check|spec|sherd|**/SPEC.md, **/*.rs|sherd check|-|-|a citation across spec nodes does not resolve
sherd-nav|spec|sherd|**/SPEC.md|sherd sync --check|sherd sync|-|a §N table is stale
sherd-budget|spec|sherd|**/SPEC.md, .context-limits|sherd budget|-|-|a spec chain is over its ceiling
flake-lock-graph|supply|jq|flake.lock|scripts/flake-lock-graph.sh {{files}}|-|-|flake.lock grew a second nixpkgs or too many nodes
deny|supply|cargo-deny|Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, deny.toml|cargo deny check --disable-fetch licenses bans|-|-|a license or ban rule failed
agents-table|spec|-|hk.pkl, AGENTS.md, scripts/agents-table.sh|scripts/agents-table.sh --check|scripts/agents-table.sh|-|AGENTS.md step table is stale
pkli-check|spec|cargo|-|cargo run -q --bin pkli -- check|-|-|a tracked file type has no row in .pklith, or a row matches nothing
gen-check|spec|cargo|.pklith, hk.pklith.pkl|cargo run -q --bin pkli -- gen --check|cargo run -q --bin pkli -- gen|-|hk.pklith.pkl no longer matches .pklith; run `pkli gen`

## types
type|checks|min|exempt
*|trailing-whitespace,final-newline,line-endings,no-bom,no-merge-conflict,no-case-conflict,no-broken-symlinks,no-large-files,no-private-key,ripsecrets,typos|-|-
rs|rustfmt,clippy,test,doctest,rustdoc,coverage,file-ceilings|-|-
nix|nixfmt|-|-
lock|flake-lock-graph|-|-
Cargo.lock|deny|-|-
toml|taplo|-|-
SPEC.md|mth-fmt,mth-check,sherd-check,sherd-nav,sherd-budget,links|-|-
md|links|-|-
sh|shellcheck|-|-
envrc|shellcheck|-|-
pre-commit|shellcheck|-|-
commit-msg|shellcheck|-|-
pre-push|shellcheck|-|-
yml|actionlint,zizmor|-|-
context-limits|sherd-budget|-|-
coverage|coverage|-|-
pkl|-|-|hk.pkl is evaluated against the vendored schema by every hk run; pkl/Config.pkl is vendored
gitignore|-|-|git configuration; hygiene steps only
LICENSE|-|-|license text, nothing to lint
pklith|pkli-check,gen-check|-|-
